  "$comment": "Sellekni design tokens — single source of truth. Edit here, run `pnpm --filter @sellekni/tokens build`. Triage colours are RESERVED for triage bands; never use them for decoration or brand. Triage markers on LIGHT surfaces MUST carry a 2px triageOutline (fills alone fail 3:1 there). Shape + letter are mandatory in every mode. Status colours (ok/warn/danger/info) are per mode, used as TEXT/ICON only, and live on hues >= 30 deg away from every triage hue (cyan/violet/magenta/blue) so a generic state can never read as a band. The LOGO is mono inside the product (logoMono); logo.red exists for the splash, store icon and pitch only and is NOT emitted to CSS: it is within RGB distance ~30 of triage R.",
